commit 0d2722acbdb0838ff9d37861628a217695c852db
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 6 20:07:00 2026 +0000

    Fail one tweet, not the batch, on a malformed embed payload
    
    An embed payload whose __typename is a list or dict raised TypeError on
    the unavailable-type membership test in parse_tweet_result. TypeError
    escapes the per-item (HttpError, ParseError) handlers, so a `tweet`
    batch stopped at the first such payload with a traceback.
    
    - parse_tweet_result only checks __typename against the unavailable
      types when it is a string; any other value is an ordinary tweet type.
    - tweet_from_body turns data-shape errors (TypeError, AttributeError,
      KeyError, IndexError) raised while parsing into a ParseError naming
      the tweet ID, chained to the original. Batch loops still catch only
      HttpError and ParseError.
    
    Tests cover list/dict __typename in the parser, the wrapping in
    tweet_from_body, and a sync and async CLI batch with a poisoned ID in
    the middle.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GFJYpdQfKM3EzC7aEPfcNk

